  "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level is ${I}^{\u2032}(t).$\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}[{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}+12] \\\\  & =2t{e}^{-t}+{t}^{2}\\cdot (-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =2t{e}^{-t}-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =t{e}^{-t}(2-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level is $t{e}^{-t}(2-t)$ hundreds of units per week.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
